  "verdict": "On the real cohort <k> and D are nearly independent (r=+0.15, VIF=1.02), so their effects separate cleanly. BOTH independently predict p_c: partial r(p_c,<k>|D)=+0.60 (p=6e-11) and partial r(p_c,D|<k>)=+0.50 (p=1e-07); mean degree is somewhat stronger. This REVISES the preliminary n=10 result (D looked irrelevant) \u2014 with n=100 and a full D range, fractal dimension is a real, independent predictor, not reducible to connectivity."
